    "faq_KrUKzc": {
      "type": "faq",
      "blocks": {
        "item_f4j7Nj": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "flow rates",
            "content": "<ul><li></li></ul>",
            "custom-html": "<p><a href=\"https://momi.baby/blogs/momtech/flow-rate\">Visit our blog for a complete guide on mōmi flow rates.</a>\n</p><p><br><span style=\"color:#ff0099;\">Important: <br>Before using the nipple for the first time, clean it with the included cleaning tool, passing the tip of the tool through the opening of the nipple duct 5 - 10 times.  This not only cleans the duct, but also establishes the nipple's correct flow rate.  Watch the demo video <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=L0SxQwt_KNQ\">here</a>.</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><b>Level 1</b> is recommended for:\n</p><ul>\n  <li>late pre-term and full-term newborns </li>\n  <li>exclusively breastfed babies up to 3 months old who are being introduced to a bottle for the first time (unless they are accustomed to nursing with a strong letdown) </li>\n  <li>babies who have established feeding skills with other brands’ level 0 (preemie, etc.)</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p> </p><p><b>Level 2</b> is recommended for:\n</p><ul>\n  <li>exclusively breastfed babies older than 3 months</li>\n  <li>exclusively breastfed babies under 3 months who have adapted to a heavy let-down</li>\n  <li>babies who have established feeding skills with other brands’ level 1 or equivalent (slow flow, etc.)</li>\n  <li>babies who have previously adapted to mōmi’s Level 1 and who have graduated to needing a faster flow rate, typically 3 months or older </li> </ul>\n\n<p> </p><p><b>Level 3</b> is recommended for:</p><ul>\n  <li>\nbabies who have established feeding skills with other brands’ level 2 or equivalent (medium flow, etc.), typically 6 months or older</li>\n  <li>babies who have previously adapted to mōmi’s Level 2 and who have graduated to needing a faster flow rate, typically 6 months or older</li>\n</ul>"
          }
        },
        "item_nmXieY": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "cleaning and assembly",
            "content": "<p>Cleaning is easy with the purple mōmi cleaning tool, included with each bottle set and replacement bundle.  The cleaning tool is inserted through the nipple’s central duct with warm soapy water.  See <a href=\"https://momi.baby/blogs/momtech/momi-getting-started\" title=\"https://momi.baby/blogs/momtech/momi-getting-started\">blog post</a> for how-to with pictures.</p><p>And assembly is as easy as 1-2-3 - just insert the nipple into the collar, and screw the collar onto the bottle.  Just three parts - no complicated pieces to clean and assemble!</p>",
            "custom-html": ""
          }
        },
        "item_pmVntC": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "mōmi bottle compatibility",
            "content": "<p>Write content to answer common questions your customers may have about your products, shipping policies, etc.</p>",
            "custom-html": "<p>mōmi's stretchy silicone requires a mōmi brand collar of the same generation as the nipple. (For more details about compatibility between gen 1 and gen 2, visit <a href=\"/pages/faq#gen2\">our faq </a>.)</p> \n\n<p>However, if you have baby bottles at home that you'd like to use with a mōmi nipple, our collar is compatible with Phillips Avent (plastic), Spectra, Maymom and Chico Duo. Customers using mōmi with other bottle bases often purchase <a href=\"/products/replacement-set\">replacement set(s) </a>, which contain everything you need to convert to mōmi using a compatible base.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_tXtLHp": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "mōmi + breastfeeding",
            "content": "<p>Write content to answer common questions your customers may have about your products, shipping policies, etc.</p>",
